{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the dispute is over the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02741 (fare ledger EV-FARE-02741, total_charged SGD 4.50, payment_status CHARGED). The ruling is that the fee is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand. POL-NS-01 allows the fee only if the driver (a) arrived, (b) was inside the pickup geofence at or before the arrival event, (c) held position for a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period in force, and (d) terminated the trip on a recognised reason code at or after the required dwell elapsed. The free waiting period for this trip is 180 seconds, read from the record's own platform_policy.free_wait_sec (EV-TRIP-02741), not from the fee_schedule defaults. The driver did arrive: the trip record carries the 'arrived' event at 18:33:47, and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02741) places him inside the STANDARD 50 m radius from that moment, so POL-NS-02 is met and the arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 (he was at the pin, min_distance_m 0.0, not more than 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or more). But limb (c) fails by the narrowest possible margin: the trace's own arithmetic gives a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 179.0 seconds, from 18:33:47 to 18:36:46, a shortfall of 1.0 second against the 180-second minimum. The platform's wait-timer events agree independently: the free-wait timer started at 18:33:49 and the trip was cancelled at 18:36:46, 177 seconds later. Under POL-NS-06 an in-geofence dwell shorter than the free waiting period makes the cancellation fee not chargeable and refundable in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages. The shortfall cannot be made up by accumulation: the trace shows a single in-geofence run (run_count 1), so POL-NS-06(i) has no second interval to add, and the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-02741-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0, which makes limb (i) unavailable rather than exonerating anyone.\n\nFor the driver. Your statement that you 'waited the free period then cancelled' is contradicted by your own trace and by the platform clock, by one second. Your claim that limb (c) was satisfied is rejected: 179 seconds is less than the 180 seconds the clause requires. Your claim that limb (d) was satisfied is also rejected: limb (d) requires termination at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed, and the cancellation at 18:36:46 fell one second before the period would have expired at 18:36:47; RIDER_NO_SHOW is a recognised reason code, but the timing condition is not met. Your point that the arrival marker is not false is accepted, but it does not help you, because POL-NS-05 does not displace the clock and the clock still runs short. Because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full, POL-NS-07 does not apply, and your claim for SGD 3.60 (80% of SGD 4.50) is refused; the anti-farming check (no_show_terminations_30d 1, 1/62 = 0.016) never comes into play because the precondition for compensation is absent. Your claim that the fare ledger reconciles is accepted (SGD 4.50 matches platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd), but a clean ledger is not a basis for the charge — the charge fails on the dwell, not on the ledger. Your claim that the rider's device sat 616.9 m to 622.3 m from the pin throughout is accepted as fact, but POL-NS-06 refunds the fee whether or not the rider was present.\n\nFor the rider. Your description of the cancellation as 'almost immediately' is not accurate — the driver held position for essentially the full free period — but your bottom line is correct, and on the strict-liability terms of POL-NS-06 the fee must be returned. Your further point that your device was stationary at the pickup is not supported: the rider track places your device roughly 620 m from the pin throughout (0 qualifying fixes out of 48), so you were not at the pickup point. That does not change the result, because POL-NS-06 refunds the fee regardless of rider presence, and POL-NS-04 does not apply here in any event: the only chat message in EV-CHAT-02741 was sent by the driver, not by you, so limb (a) of that clause is not met. The amount refunded is the cancellation-fee line only — SGD 4.50 — with no booking or platform fee in the ledger.\n\nConfidence and procedure. The two artifacts that carry the deciding dwell fact — the GPS trace and the trip record — both stand at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; no artifact the ruling rests on is below 1.0. No POL-NS-08 impairment applies: there is no clock skew (the arrived event sits on a trace fix), no gap over 120 seconds, the chat count matches the trip record, and the fare line reconciles. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, there are no counterparty disputes in the trailing 90 days, and the anti-farming check is not tripped. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold. Two claims that cited the MISSING advisory were discarded at the citation stage and are recorded below; their exclusion does not change the outcome, the limb being unavailable either way. No referral is issued: none of the referral-producing clauses is engaged — the arrival marker is not false (POL-NS-05(ii)), there is no route deviation (POL-RD-06(c)), no billing-integrity question (POL-RD-09(4)) and no anti-farming escalation (POL-NS-07)."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Nor can the driver invoke the traffic-advisory qualification in POL-NS-06(i): the only advisory artifact for this pickup road, EV-ADVIS-02741-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0, and POL-NS-06(i) requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated. A MISSING advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and cannot be asserted to excuse the shortfall.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02741-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The traffic advisory artifact is MISSING — no advisory covers Blk 108 Yishun Ring Rd in this window — so POL-NS-06(i) cannot be run and no accumulation of separate in-geofence intervals is available. I do not assert it; the absence is cited only to record that the limb is unavailable, and the dwell is measured on the single 179-second run.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02741-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
